{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgF11Rqe2moBbb4JwmXFH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug, and all 6 tests pass (`python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`).\n\n`parse_price` in `inventory.py` now strips commas when they are thousands separators. A comma counts as a thousands separator when it sits in groups of three digits and is followed by a decimal part or by another comma group. `\"1,234.50\"` now returns `1234.5`, and `\"$1,234,567\"` returns `1234567.0`.\n\n`\"12.50\"`, `\"$3\"` and `\"12,50\"` behave as before, and I left `total_value` alone.\n\nI added regression tests in `tests/test_inventory.py` for `\"1,234.50\"`, `\"$1,234,567\"` and `\"1,234,567.89\"`.\n\nA bare `\"1,234\"` still parses as the European decimal `1.234`, because the issue's rule only treats a comma as a thousands separator when a dot or another comma group follows. If you want it read as 1234, the issue would need to say so.\n\nI haven't committed anything."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":170,"cache_read_input_tokens":25486,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":170},"output_tokens":326,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0db71f2f-152c-41a5-bba4-93e6114c60cb","uuid":"2cd465b0-c8ef-4c4e-983d-18a203dcb355","timestamp":"2026-10-21T07:38:21.030Z","request_id":"req_011CgF11RFfAxzFZ6rjwXmLQ"}
